# Python build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Secrets and local caches — must never be committed (defense in depth)
.valoria_pat
*.pat
.valoria_cache.json
.valoria_lane

# Machine-local Claude Code overrides (shared config lives in .claude/settings.json)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Generated simulation run output — never committed (mirrors sim/results/'s convention)
tools/sim_harness/results/

# Repository State Armature — generated, head-sha-bearing; regenerated by review_core/refresh, not committed in Phase 1 (ED-IN-0077)
tools/observability/review_state.json
tools/observability/review_state_data.js

# Agent-isolation worktrees (transient harness machinery, never repo content)
.claude/worktrees/
.coverage

# Generated by tools/evacuation_plan.py --json. Regenerable; not committed (no round-trip
# gate yet, and committing an unguarded generated snapshot is the stale-artifact hazard
# ED-IN-0126 exists to avoid).
references/evacuation_manifest.json

# ── GENERATED LAYER — untracked 2026-08-22 (culling wave 5, ED-IN-0194) ────────────────────────
# These are BUILT from tracked sources, never authored. Committing them made every prose edit a
# diff in files no human wrote: adding ONE document to proposals/ churned three of these indexes
# and turned a blocking gate red. Two sibling branches once collided on 18 files "over nothing" —
# every conflict a generated file, zero in source.
#
# THE GATE FLIP THAT MAKES THIS SAFE: their `--check` modes existed to detect a STALE COMMITTED
# COPY. With nothing committed there is no staleness to detect, so the tests now BUILD the artifact
# from source and assert on the result. `tests/valoria/conftest.py`'s `generated_layer` fixture is
# the single owner of the build ORDER (key_graph -> engine_atlas/contract_index), because two of
# these builders read another's output.
#
# ⚠ NOT UNTRACKED, AND DO NOT ADD THEM: `engine/engine_params/*.json` and `params_tables.yaml`.
# Those are RUNTIME INPUTS — `engine/substrate/descriptors.py` and `keys.py` read them at import,
# so an untracked clone would not start. `params_tables.yaml` is additionally NOT REGENERABLE (its
# source docs were evacuated), making it a source rather than an artifact.
systems/*/_identifier_census.yaml
references/identifier_census.json
references/key_graph.json
references/execution_map.json
references/EXECUTION_MAP.md
references/execution_trace.json
references/engine_atlas.json
references/ENGINE_ATLAS.md
references/CONTRACT_INDEX.md
references/KEY_INDEX.md
references/definitions/definitions.yaml
